## 3 · Invariants — violating any of these loses marks or worse

Restated from `CLAUDE.md` because they must survive being read in isolation.

**Product (`BRIEF-02`–`BRIEF-05`)**
- **MVVM is mandatory** — Models / Views / ViewModels / persistence & data services clearly separated.
- **SwiftUI-primary; GameKit & SpriteKit are outside the taught scope** (use at own risk, unsupported).
- The cultural element must **shape gameplay mechanics**, not decorate them — the top rubric criterion's Excellent test is "could not be transferred to an unrelated subject without the game breaking."
- **Five required views** (Menu, Game, Leaderboard, How To Play, Settings), ≥3 distinct animations in Game View, registration/login/logout + profiles, CRUD + **cloud sync**, **two Week 7 industry requirements**.
- Works on **iPhone 17 / 17 Pro / 17 Pro Max / 11-inch iPad Air**, both system light & dark modes; marked on **Xcode 26.4.1 / iOS 26.4.1 / iPhone 17 Pro simulator**.

**Process (`BRIEF-01`, `BRIEF-06`, `BRIEF-07`)**
- Work **only** in the assigned private repo under `rmit-vietnam-computing-technologies` — never personal/public repos; ZIP must equal the final commit.
- Exact deliverable names: `SourceCode/`, `Document.pdf`, `GitHub.txt`, `Youtube.txt`.
- **All 5 members appear and speak in the video** or that member scores zero for the presentation component.
- Commit history is assessment evidence — regular commits from **every** member across the whole window.

**Phase**
- **The concept is settled** (`DEC-01`): a swipe-decision card game about **nghề làm tranh dân gian Đông Hồ**, played as one craft household across a single 36-card run, won by preparation rather than by stats. Do not re-argue it.
- **Names, roles, persistence stack, industry requirements and workload split are open.** Do not present those as chosen; route "what did we decide?" to `DEC-01`.

---

## 4 · Keeping the KB true

Any change must be reflected in the KB in the same turn:

| Change | Update |
| --- | --- |
| A decision closes (concept, roles, names, stack…) | `DEC-01` (status + date + rationale) → `BUILD-01` → seed `DES-xx`/`DATA-xx` when design begins |
| Project/repo state changes (repo cloned, Xcode project created, code written) | `BUILD-01` |
| The plan changes or a milestone passes | `BUILD-02` |
| A meeting happens | `BUILD-03` (retire/replace the agenda) + `DEC-01` |
| A file added, moved or removed | frontmatter + `.claude/context-index.md` §1–2 + the `CLAUDE.md` router |

**A KB that silently drifts is worse than no KB** — it converts uncertainty into confident error. If you cannot verify a "reality" claim, say so rather than repeating it.
